  "answer": "Password cracking primarily involves adversaries attempting to guess a password by trying every possible combination until they succeed. This method is known as a brute force attack. It is computationally feasible and guarantees success as it systematically goes through all potential passwords based on the character set used (including lower case letters, upper case letters, numbers, and symbols) and the maximum length of the password [Source 1].\n\nAdditionally, adversaries may employ brute force techniques to access accounts when they do not know the passwords or when they have obtained password hashes. This process involves systematically guessing the password using a repetitive or iterative mechanism, often through interaction with a service that validates the credentials [Source 2]. Brute forcing can occur at various stages during a breach, leveraging information gathered from other activities within the compromised environment [Source 3].",
